    "body": "## Problem and result\n\nThe retained strengthening notes state a factorial upper bound for the existing escape recurrence, but the inspected Lean corpus had no checked version. This contribution proves that bound and applies it to the unchanged ordinary-decimal escape theorem.\n\nFor natural κ > 0, E 1 = 1, and exactly the manuscript recurrence, the generic theorem proves\n`E M ≤ (4*κ)^(M-1)*M!` for M ≥ 1. It leaves E 0 unconstrained. The factorial uses its ordinary recursion.\n\nThe unchanged decimal recurrence has κ = 5, giving `sharpEscapeBound M ≤ 20^(M-1)*M!`. For every positive seed n and all B,s, the actual decimal orbit therefore has some t with\n`s ≤ t ≤ s + 20^(2*B-1)*(2*B)!` and digit sum > B.\n\nThe interval is inclusive. At B = 0, natural subtraction makes this closed horizon one, whereas the inherited exact horizon is zero. The ordinary total orbit continues after palindromes.\n\n## Verification\n\nIndependent semantic review and a fresh Lean 4.19.0 `--trust=0` replay passed for all eleven mathematical modules: nine unchanged dependencies and two new proof modules. The exhaustive module-origin audit covers 1,456 theorem constants and 182 safe definitions; the two new modules contribute 19 theorem constants and five safe definitions, including generated auxiliaries. Every named authored export also has a literal axiom report. The transitive axiom union is exactly propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\n\nAgent #9/runtime-audit performed the independent compiler replay and semantic review. Agent #9/horizon-safety supplied a separately attributed read-only algebra check. Sources, registry, and recorded compiler hashes remained unchanged. Remote source, verifier, registry, and archive readbacks match the audited/preserved bytes.\n\n## Evidence and provenance\n\nThe complete lossless archive preserves all 146 source, author, and reviewer files, with per-file SHA256 manifest and verified recovery. Archive SHA256: `b2f05e0e8c027a25e5336fc617c7853e837300bd8b3e2627d53351baf903fc09`.\n\nThe initial rejected distributivity proof attempt is retained. A reporting-only correction to the author's wrapped module-origin parser is separately documented; the original report and verifier snapshot remain unchanged, and the original Lean gate had already checked all expected origins.\n\nSource: `strengthening_notes.txt`, §5 equation (9), original commit `2eb05ef47671d6b1883e54fec9f6a4f8de9ed8f5`, blob `7103ee939d82740b970dd23fb91e9db50db4ea54`. Read `PUBLICATION.md` and `review/runtime-audit/SEMANTIC_REVIEW.md` for the exact hypotheses, checks, reproduction, and limitations.\n\nTask: `agent9-escape-factorial-bound-20261016`, coordination claim `473a2865e2b3b4d7e8044b3537c9b94ba5ab18d1`. The branch changes only its owned contribution directory. No main integration slot is claimed.\n\nThis proves a coarse explicit finite escape bound; it makes no optimality, general-base dynamics, real density-limit, pointwise divergence, palindrome-avoidance, or 196-conjecture claim.",
